References: <8a0a8c3c1003171730m9ff2787y43d1fe2b17e760ce@mail.gmail.com> <839691711003171759mf429a48r3d9f91c773f7abb4@mail.gmail.com> <8a0a8c3c1003171808h26c9c5f8oee6a01f8edba89e8@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <839691711003171819ne986227ib821d35625a75517@mail.gmail.com>

Hi Sivan,

Typically, the length of the chain indicated how much information is
in the missing part of your data. So, lower chain lengths are
generally better and 4-6 are fairly short chains. Chains in large,
complicated datasets can easily reach into the hundreds or thousands.

Cheers,
matt.

